          "id": "india-modi-gold-appeal-2026-11-22",
          "headline": "Modi says buying less gold, as he asked, has helped bring prices down",
          "summary": "Speaking in Lucknow, Prime Minister Narendra Modi thanked people for cutting gold purchases after his appeal, made when the West Asia war pushed up oil prices and strained forex reserves. All India Radio reports 24-carat gold fell to ₹12,523 a gram on Saturday from ₹15,250 on May 9, and gold imports dropped nearly 40% in April to October.",
          "why_it_matters": "Lower gold imports ease pressure on India's trade deficit and the rupee.",
          "importance": 3,
          "lead": false,
          "verified": false,
          "note": "Single source: All India Radio.",
