          "id": "world-cop31-overtime-2026-11-20",
          "headline": "Update: COP31 nears a final deal that still leaves out fossil fuels",
          "summary": "A new draft was released on Sunday in Antalya, two days after the summit was due to end, and COP31 president Murat Kurum called delegates back to approve it. The text does not name fossil fuels; it only points back to the 2023 Dubai agreement to move away from them. It keeps a goal for carbon capture at gigatonne scale by 2035 and a call to at least triple adaptation finance by 2035. Whether it was adopted was not yet known at the time of writing.",
